  "prompt": "Find the exact value of $\\cot 30^\\circ$. Write it using \"sqrt\", for example \"sqrt(2)/2\".",
  "answerType": "expression",
  "primaryAnswer": "sqrt(3)",
  "alternativeAnswers": [
    "3^(1/2)",
    "sqrt3",
    "√3",
    "sqrt(3)/1"
  ],
  "acceptanceMode": "normalized",
  "hint": "$\\cot\\theta = \\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}$ — cosine on top this time.",
  "hints": [
    {
      "level": "nudge",
      "text": "$\\cot\\theta = \\frac{\\cos\\theta}{\\sin\\theta}$ — cosine on top this time."
    },
    {
      "level": "guide",
      "text": "$\\cos 30^\\circ = \\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}$ and $\\sin 30^\\circ = \\frac{1}{2}$."
    },
    {
      "level": "reveal",
      "text": "$\\frac{\\sqrt{3}/2}{1/2} = \\sqrt{3}$."
    }
  ],
  "explanation": [
    "Cotangent is cosine over sine: $\\cot 30^\\circ = \\frac{\\cos 30^\\circ}{\\sin 30^\\circ}$.",
    "Substitute the special values: $\\frac{\\sqrt{3}/2}{1/2}$.",
    "The halves cancel, leaving $\\sqrt{3}$."
  ],
  "alternativeExplanations": [
    {
      "title": "Flip the tangent",
      "steps": [
        "$\\tan 30^\\circ = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}$, and cotangent is its reciprocal.",
        "Flipping gives $\\cot 30^\\circ = \\sqrt{3} \\approx 1.732$.",
        "That is bigger than $1$, which makes sense: a shallow $30^\\circ$ ramp runs much further than it rises."
      ]
    }
  ],
